# Scratch/exploratory
scratch/

# Rust build artifacts
rust_core/target/

# Exploratory scripts at the repo root are ignored by pattern, not by name.
# The seven name-specific rules that used to live here (/bank_evaluation*.py,
# /device_evaluation*.py, /eval_conmute*.py, /go_vs_python.py,
# /language_evaluation.py, /test_ahp.py, /generic_template.py) are gone: all
# seven named files from the 2026 reorganization plan that was never executed,
# so they protected nothing. /test_ahp.py was worse than dead — a real, tracked
# test with that exact name lives in src/decision_maker/tests/, and being
# root-anchored the rule never matched it, so it looked like a protection while
# covering none. `/scratch/`, `/*.db` and `*.py[cod]` below do the actual work.
/*.db
violations*.txt
.agents/

# Obsidian vault — the vault root is docs/, never the repo root.
# A .obsidian/ at the repo root makes Obsidian treat the whole repository as the
# vault, which puts results/, .venv/ and src/ in the graph. Keep it in docs/.
/.obsidian/

# Vendored plugin build artifacts. manifest.json IS tracked: it is the source of
# truth for which plugin and which version, and without it a fresh clone silently
# has no plugins. main.js and styles.css are ~1MB of generated code per plugin.
/docs/.obsidian/plugins/*/main.js
/docs/.obsidian/plugins/*/styles.css
/docs/.obsidian/plugins/*/node_modules/
